Do not restore x18 in longjmp on arm64 in the ANDRUNA build.

On Windows ARM64, x18 always points to the thread environment block, and
a fault taken with another value in x18 ends the process. bionic's
longjmp restores the low bits of x18 (the shadow call stack pointer) from
the jmp_buf. The ANDRUNA build has no shadow call stack (patch 0004), so
x18 is left alone; setjmp still stores the value, and the jmp_buf layout
is unchanged.

diff --git a/libc/arch-arm64/bionic/setjmp.S b/libc/arch-arm64/bionic/setjmp.S
--- a/libc/arch-arm64/bionic/setjmp.S
+++ b/libc/arch-arm64/bionic/setjmp.S
@@ -253,9 +253,11 @@ L(load_registers):
   m_unmangle_registers x2, sp_reg=x10
   mov sp, x10

+#if !defined(ANDRUNA)
   // Restore the low bits of the shadow call stack pointer.
   and x18, x18, #~SCS_MASK
   orr x18, x3, x18
+#endif

   // Restore floating point registers.
   ldp d14, d15, [x0, #(_JB_D14_D15 * 8)]
